  "summary": "Mask R-CNN extends Faster R-CNN with a parallel fully convolutional branch that predicts a binary mask per class for each RoI, and replaces quantized RoIPool with a quantization-free RoIAlign layer so that features align pixel-to-pixel with the input.",
  "problemSummary": "Instance segmentation must detect every object and precisely segment each instance, but the prevailing Faster R-CNN pipeline was not designed for pixel-to-pixel alignment: RoIPool quantizes coordinates, causing misalignment that hurts pixel-accurate masks, while per-pixel multi-class softmax couples segmentation with classification.",
