  "summary": "Soft-NMS replaces NMS's hard zeroing step with a continuous re-scoring rule: the scores of boxes overlapping the selected box M are decayed by a linear or Gaussian function of their IoU with M, implemented as a one-line change to greedy NMS with no retraining and the same complexity.",
  "problemSummary": "Greedy non-maximum suppression is a hard-threshold post-processing step that zeroes the scores of neighboring detections, so any object that overlaps the kept box above the threshold is missed, while a fixed threshold tuned for one evaluation overlap degrades average precision at other thresholds.",
  "contributions": [
   "Decay the classification scores of overlapping detections as a continuous (linear or Gaussian) function of their IoU with the current top box instead of setting them to zero.",
   "linear re-scoring: si = si * (1 - iou(M, bi)) for iou >= Nt",
   "Gaussian re-scoring: si = si * exp(-iou(M, bi)^2 / sigma) for boxes not yet selected",
   "one-line modification of the greedy NMS pseudo-code",
   "no extra training and no change to the detector"
  ],
  "limitations": [
   "Soft-NMS remains greedy and does not find the globally optimal re-scoring of detection boxes.",
   "Adds a sigma hyper-parameter that needs tuning (performance varies across sigma values).",
   "Gains shrink to 0.5% for non proposal-based detectors like SSD and YOLOv2.",
   "Only PASCAL VOC 2007 and MS-COCO are evaluated."
  ],
