  "summary": "The paper proposes KL Loss, which models the predicted box coordinate as a Gaussian and the ground truth as a Dirac delta, then regresses via the KL divergence so each coordinate also predicts its own variance. The learned variance is used at test time by var voting, which refines the selected box's location as a variance-weighted vote over its neighbors inside NMS/soft-NMS.",
  "problemSummary": "Ground-truth boxes in large-scale detection datasets are inherently ambiguous (inaccurate labeling, occlusion, fuzzy object boundaries), yet the standard smooth L1 box regression loss treats every target as equally certain. In addition, detectors assume a high classification score implies accurate localization, so NMS can keep poorly localized high-scoring boxes while discarding accurate low-scoring ones.",
  "contributions": [
   "Predict a per-coordinate Gaussian localization distribution trained with a KL-divergence regression loss, then use the predicted variances to vote the location of each kept box during NMS.",
   "Gaussian parameterization of predicted box coordinates (mean and standard deviation from an extra FC layer on fc7)",
   "KL divergence regression loss that learns box transformation and localization variance jointly",
   "alpha = log(sigma^2) parameterization to avoid exploding gradients early in training",
   "var voting: variance-weighted coordinate voting over neighbors during NMS/soft-NMS",
   "smooth-L1-style tail of the loss for large residuals",
   "random Gaussian initialization of the variance head so training starts like smooth L1"
  ],
  "limitations": [
   "Var voting needs a tunable parameter sigma_t: AP75/AP80/AP90 shift noticeably as it varies, with acceptable values only around 0.005 to 0.05.",
   "Overall AP50 improvement from var voting is tiny (0.1%), so most of the benefit shows up only in strict high-IoU metrics.",
   "The distribution model is simplified to independent univariate Gaussians per coordinate rather than a full joint distribution.",
   "The method is built on and evaluated with two-stage Faster R-CNN / Mask R-CNN fast R-CNN heads."
  ],
