  "summary": "GFL replaces the separate quality branch with a joint classification-IoU representation (soft target y in [0,1] at the ground-truth class index) optimized by Quality Focal Loss, and models each box coordinate as a discretized General distribution over n+1 bins sharpened by Distribution Focal Loss; both are special cases of one continuous-label Generalized Focal Loss.",
  "problemSummary": "Dense one-stage detectors estimate localization quality (IoU/centerness) in a separate branch that is trained independently but multiplied with the classification score only at inference, and is supervised on positives only, so unreliable negatives can outrank true positives in NMS. Separately, boxes are modeled as rigid Dirac delta (or Gaussian) distributions that cannot express annotation ambiguity and uncertainty.",
  "contributions": [
   "Merge localization quality into the class-score vector and learn a discretized probability distribution over box coordinates, optimizing both with a continuous-label generalization of Focal Loss.",
   "classification-IoU joint representation with continuous quality targets (negatives supervised at 0)",
   "Quality Focal Loss (QFL) extending Focal Loss to continuous labels with modulating factor |y - sigma|^beta",
   "General distribution over discretized box-coordinate range implemented with an (n+1)-unit softmax",
   "Distribution Focal Loss (DFL) enlarging the probabilities of the two bins nearest the target coordinate",
   "regression branch last layer outputs n+1 logits per box direction instead of 1 (negligible extra cost)",
   "quality scores additionally weight the GIoU and DFL box losses during training"
  ],
  "limitations": [
   "Post-processing is unchanged: threshold filtering plus class-wise NMS at IoU 0.6 still produce the final detections.",
   "Absolute gains are incremental (about 0.6-1 AP) over already strong one-stage baselines such as ATSS.",
   "The approach requires tuning several hyper-parameters: QFL beta, distribution bins n and interval delta, and loss balance weights.",
   "Validation is limited to COCO and dense one-stage detectors; other datasets and detector families are not evaluated."
  ],
