  "summary": "PP-YOLOE evolves PP-YOLOv2 into an anchor-free, scalable, deployment-friendly detector: a CSPRepResNet backbone and neck built from re-parameterizable RepResBlocks with width/depth multipliers, Task Alignment Learning for dynamic label assignment, an Efficient Task-aligned Head (ET-head) with ESE attention, and varifocal plus distribution focal losses.",
  "problemSummary": "Industrial real-time detectors must simultaneously improve accuracy, speed and hardware deployability; the anchor-based PP-YOLOv2 baseline relies on hand-crafted anchor hyperparameters and operators like deformable convolution and Matrix NMS that hurt portability, while classification and localization tasks conflict in the head.",
  "contributions": [
   "Drop anchors and hardware-unfriendly operators, replace the backbone/neck with re-parameterizable RepResBlocks scaled by multipliers, align classification and localization via TAL, and train with quality-aware VFL/DFL losses in a unified ET-head.",
   "anchor-free assignment following FCOS anchor points with upper/lower feature-map bounds",
   "RepResBlock re-parameterized to a basic residual block at inference, used in CSPRepResNet backbone and CSPRepResStage neck",
   "width multiplier and depth multiplier to scale s/m/l/x variants",
   "Task Alignment Learning (TAL): dynamic label assignment plus task-aligned loss",
   "Efficient Task-aligned Head (ET-head) with ESE channel attention and DFL alignment",
   "varifocal loss (VFL) for classification and distribution focal loss (DFL) for box distribution"
  ],
  "limitations": [
   "Anchor-free assignment loses 0.3 AP because upper/lower bounds only approximately match the anchor-based assignment of PP-YOLOv2.",
   "The ET-head increases latency by 0.9 ms on a V100 relative to the previous head.",
   "Only COCO single-scale results are reported; no robustness, domain-shift, or small-object stress analysis beyond COCO APS is given.",
   "Comparison fairness is limited by mixed engines (Paddle inference vs official codebases) and re-evaluated YOLOv5/YOLOX."
  ],
