  "summary": "ViTDet adapts a plain ViT to detection only at fine-tuning time: a simple feature pyramid built by parallel strided convolutions/deconvolutions from the single 1/16-scale last feature map (no FPN top-down/lateral connections), non-overlapping window attention for high-resolution maps with a few (default 4) evenly placed cross-window propagation blocks (global attention or zero-initialized conv residual blocks), and standard Mask R-CNN/Cascade heads on MAE-pre-trained ViT-B/L/H backbones.",
  "problemSummary": "Object detection has been built around hierarchical, multi-scale backbones because ConvNets are hierarchical, which entrenched FPN-style neck/head designs; the plain (non-hierarchical, single-scale) ViT is hard to fine-tune for detection because it lacks multi-scale maps, global self-attention over high-resolution images is prohibitive, and redesigning backbones into hierarchies couples pre-training to detection.",
  "contributions": [
   "Keep the original ViT architecture untouched by pre-training, then add only minimal fine-tuning-time modules: a simple single-scale-origin pyramid, window attention with sparse cross-window propagation, and conventional detection heads.",
   "simple feature pyramid from the last 1/16 feature map, producing scales {1/32, 1/16, 1/8, 1/4} via parallel stride-{2, 1, 1/2, 1/4} convolutions/deconvolutions (fractional stride = deconvolution)",
   "non-overlapping window self-attention during fine-tuning, without Swin-style shifting",
   "4 cross-window propagation blocks placed evenly: global self-attention in the last block of each subset, or added conv residual blocks initialized to identity",
   "MAE pre-training on ImageNet-1K without labels as the backbone initialization",
   "Mask R-CNN / Cascade Mask R-CNN / RetinaNet heads with large-scale jittering at 1024x1024 input",
   "relative position biases added only during fine-tuning for comparisons"
  ],
  "limitations": [
   "Global self-attention in all 24 ViT-L blocks requires special memory optimization and is impractical for scaling to larger models such as ViT-H.",
   "Exploiting the long-tailed class distribution of LVIS (e.g., CLIP text embeddings, rare-class techniques) is beyond the scope of the study.",
   "Exploring detectors with even fewer inductive biases (beyond standard Mask R-CNN heads) is left as open future work."
  ],
