  "summary": "RT-DETR is a real-time end-to-end detector with an efficient hybrid encoder that decouples intra-scale interaction (AIFI, self-attention on the highest-level feature only) from cross-scale fusion (CCFF, CNN/RepConv blocks), plus uncertainty-minimal query selection that explicitly minimizes the discrepancy between localization and classification predictions of selected encoder features.",
  "problemSummary": "YOLO-style real-time detectors depend on NMS post-processing whose two thresholds slow inference and destabilize speed and accuracy, while DETR-family detectors eliminate NMS but are too computationally expensive for real time; existing query selection also picks encoder features by classification score alone, ignoring localization quality.",
  "contributions": [
   "Replace the multi-scale Transformer encoder with a hybrid AIFI+CCFF encoder and select decoder queries by explicitly minimizing epistemic uncertainty between localization and classification heads.",
   "efficient hybrid encoder: AIFI (attention-based intra-scale interaction on S5) and CCFF (CNN-based cross-scale fusion with RepConv fusion blocks)",
   "uncertainty-minimal query selection over the top-300 encoder features",
   "Transformer decoder with auxiliary prediction heads and bipartite matching",
   "flexible speed tuning by changing the number of decoder layers without retraining",
   "scaled RT-DETR variants using ResNet-18/34/50/101 backbones"
  ],
  "limitations": [
   "Small-object accuracy remains inferior to strong real-time YOLO detectors (RT-DETR-R50 is 0.5% AP lower on AP_S than YOLOv8-L; R101 is 0.9% lower than YOLOv7-X on AP_S).",
   "Speed still depends on TensorRT FP16 deployment and on choosing how many decoder layers to run.",
   "NMS-free post-processing replaces two NMS thresholds with a score threshold that still needs scenario-specific tuning."
  ],
