  "problemSummary": "The paper argues that real-time detectors still handle scale poorly: multi-branch CSP/ELAN blocks produce homogenized inter-branch features, Res2Net-style hierarchy leaks contaminative spatial information, and homogeneous per-stage kernel sizes prevent cheap use of large receptive fields.",
