  "summary": "Grounding DINO 1.5 is a two-model suite: Pro scales the Grounding DINO architecture with a ViT-L backbone and early fusion trained on Grounding-20M (over 20M grounding-annotated images), while Edge replaces the feature enhancer with an efficient one that fuses only P5 features (vanilla self-attention plus cross-scale fusion of P3/P4) on an EfficientViT-L1 backbone, both trained on the same data.",
  "problemSummary": "Open-set detectors built on Grounding DINO still fall short on generalization across diverse categories, and their multi-scale features plus heavy feature enhancer make them impractical for real-time/edge deployment where compute resources are limited; early-fusion designs also trade higher recall for object hallucinations.",
