  "summary": "A training-only distillation framework aligning the detector's AIFI output feature F5 with frozen DINOv3 teacher features via a Deep Semantic Injector (linear projector + cosine loss), plus Gradient-guided Adaptive Modulation that tunes the loss weight from gradient-norm ratios.",
  "problemSummary": "Real-time detectors trade feature quality for speed, and RT-DETR's AIFI output is only indirectly supervised, creating a semantic bottleneck; transferring foundation-model semantics is hard because teachers and resource-constrained detectors differ in architecture and learning objective.",
  "contributions": [
   "Inject VFM semantics into the AIFI output feature F5 during training only, with an adaptively weighted alignment loss so the detector architecture and inference cost stay unchanged.",
   "Deep Semantic Injector (DSI), a training-only module supervising F5",
   "linear Feature Projector aligning resolution and channels with the teacher",
   "cosine similarity alignment loss between projected detector and teacher features",
   "Gradient-guided Adaptive Modulation (GAM) adjusting the loss weight by AIFI gradient-norm ratio",
   "unchanged architecture and inference pipeline at deployment"
  ],
  "limitations": [
   "Empirical scope is COCO 2017 with RT-DETR-based detectors (plus a few DETR baselines for ablation)",
   "DSI without GAM gives only slight improvements (about +0.1 to +0.2 AP)",
   "Training requires a pre-trained frozen DINOv3-ViT-B teacher, adding training-time cost",
   "DEIMv2-X still surpasses RT-DETRv4-X in AP, though at higher latency"
  ],
